 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<table class=\"mini\"><thead><tr><th>You have</th><th>Vinegar</th><th>+ Water</th><th>Sugar</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rice vinegar (~4.5%)</td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"30\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">30 ml</span>)</span></td><td>—</td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"8\" data-s=\"0\">8 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">2 tsp</span>)</span></td></tr><tr><td>Korean brewed vinegar 양조식초 (~7%)</td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1.25\" data-s=\"0\">1¼ tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"19\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">19 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"11\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">11 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"10\" data-s=\"0\">10 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2.5\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">2½ tsp</span>)</span></td></tr><tr><td>Table vinegar 9%</td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"15\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">15 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"15\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">15 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"10\" data-s=\"0\">10 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2.5\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">2½ tsp</span>)</span></td></tr><tr><td>Vinegar 6%</td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1.5\" data-s=\"0\">1½ tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"22\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">22 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1.5\" data-s=\"0\">1½ tsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"8\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">8 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"10\" data-s=\"0\">10 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2.5\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">2½ tsp</span>)</span></td></tr><tr><td>White / distilled vinegar 5%</td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1.75\" data-s=\"0\">1¾ tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"27\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">27 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ tsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"3\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">3 ml</span>)</span></td><td><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"10\" data-s=\"0\">10 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2.5\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">2½ tsp</span>)</span></td></tr></tbody></table>Matched to rice vinegar’s ~4.5% acidity for the marinade. Non-rice vinegars are sharper and less rounded, hence the extra sugar — taste and adjust.",
   "title_html": "Vinegar conversions (in place of the marinade’s 2 tbsp rice vinegar)"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li><b>양조식초</b> (brewed vinegar, ~6–7%) is the one the 7% row means.</li><li><b>2배식초 / 3배식초</b> are double / triple strength — use half / a third of the 7% amount and make up the rest with water.</li><li><b>빙초산</b> is glacial acetic acid (~99%): never use it as-is.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Reading Korean vinegar labels"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>It already contains sugar and salt.</li><li>Use <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tbsp</span> straight in the marinade, keep the mirin, and skip the sugar.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Seasoned rice vinegar (sushi vinegar)?"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Usukuchi (light) soy is saltier but paler than regular soy — it seasons without darkening the cucumber.</li><li>Regular soy works; use a little less.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Light soy"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>For a soaking-style pickle, see <a href=\"radish-pickle.html\">pickled radishes</a>.</p>",
   "title_html": "Radish too"
  }
 ],
