 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Slice the cucumber about <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 mm</span></b> thick (a mandoline makes this quick).</li><li>Peeling a few stripes off first looks nice but is optional.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Slice thin",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Slice about 2 mm thin — fingertips tucked.",
      "src": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/1-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/1.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Slice thin",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"250\">250 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Cucumber"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Toss with <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ tsp</span> salt and leave 10 minutes to pull the water out.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Salt and rest",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Toss with the salt and leave 10 minutes.",
      "src": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/2-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/2.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>10 min</span>",
   "title": "Salt and rest",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\">½ tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Fine salt, for drawing out water"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Rinse the salt off under cold water, then <b>squeeze firmly</b> by the handful — this is what keeps them crunchy and stops them watering down the marinade.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rinse and squeeze",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Rinse, then squeeze firmly by the handful.",
      "src": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/3-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~2 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~2 min</span>",
   "title": "Rinse and squeeze",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Add the grated ginger and garlic and the <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span> rice vinegar. Mix it up.</p>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Ginger, garlic, rice vinegar",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Grate the ginger and garlic finely, straight over the cucumber.",
      "src": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/4-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~1 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min</span>",
   "title": "Ginger, garlic, rice vinegar",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Ginger, grated"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-f=\"clove|cloves\" data-n=\"1\">1 small clove</span>",
     "name_html": "Garlic, grated"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Rice vinegar (first splash)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Stir until the sugar dissolves:<ul class=\"ing\"><li><span data-v=\"name_lc\">rice vinegar</span><span data-v-show=\"water\"> + water</span></li><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"15\" data-alt=\"1\">15 ml</span>)</span> — half the vinegar</span></li><li>sugar <span class=\"amt\"><span data-v=\"sugar\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"8\">8 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-alt=\"1\">2 tsp</span>)</span></span></span></li></ul></li><li>Pour it over the cucumbers and toss.</li><li>Optional: microwave the mirin and sugar together for 20–30 seconds first to dissolve the sugar and cook off the mirin’s alcohol; let it cool before adding.</li><li>Keeping a jar of the mix in the fridge? See <a href=\"#batch\">Make a big batch</a> for the amounts.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "The marinade",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Stir until the sugar dissolves, then pour over and toss.",
      "src": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/5-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/cucumber-sunomono/5.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~2 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~2 min</span>",
   "title": "The marinade",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span data-v=\"amount\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\">2 tbsp</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"30\" data-alt=\"1\">30 ml</span>)</span></span>",
     "name_html": "<span data-v=\"name\">Rice vinegar</span>"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span data-v=\"water\">—</span>",
     "name_html": "<span data-v-row=\"water\">Water</span>"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Chill <b>10 minutes</b> (crispest) up to <b>1 hour</b>.</li><li>Add the <b>light soy sauce and sesame</b> at the end, just before serving.</li><li>Keeps 2–3 days in the fridge, softening as it sits.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
